time=2026-10-27T03:34:42.876Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-1a5d2549 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nThe provenance init command (blueprint cd565bb0, approved by provisio-mgr 01M520Q7DAWH), in two files.\n\nWiring, cmd/provenance/init_cmd.go (cobra package): a top-level command, use \"init\", short \"Scaffold provenance in a new project\", arity none. Flags, none with a short form or default:\n- dir (string): \"Project directory (default: the current directory)\"\n- force (bool): \"Overwrite an existing .provenance.yml (the old one is saved as .provenance.yml.bak)\"\n\nInit also writes the generated-file lines to .gitattributes through ensureGitattributes (blueprint prov-2026-c896ac2d, helper in gitattributes_run.go), reported as a status line like the other files; runInit gets exactly the four lines shown before the \"Initialised\" message.\n\nLogic, cmd/provenance/init_run.go (go package, package main). Declarations in this order: const initConfig (one setConst), then the functions below. The const is a Go string built as in the original: a raw string literal (backquotes) whose content is exactly the text shown below, byte for byte, where every backquote character inside the text is written by closing the raw literal and splicing in \"`\" (that is: ` + \"`\" + `), and the text ends with the final newline shown. initConfig text:\n    # provenance configuration, written by `provenance init`.\n\n    # How strictly records are enforced: none, warn or strict. Start with warn; move to\n    # strict when your records have specs and you want violations to fail lint and commits.\n    enforcement: warn\n\n    # Where the records live, relative to this file.\n    dir: provenance\n\n    # Paths that need no record: exact paths, directory prefixes, globs or /regex/.\n    exclude_paths: ['.gitignore', 'README.md', '.provenance.yml', '.gitattributes']\n\n    # Records of other repositories that yours may implement (read-only; `provenance sync`\n    # fetches them). Example:\n    #   shared_repos:\n    #     - name: shared\n    #       url: git@github.com:your-org/shared.git\n    #       ref: main\n    shared_repos: []\n\n    # Minutes a shared-repo cache stays fresh (0 means the default, 60).\n    cache_ttl_minutes: 0\n\n    # true: a commit that changes governed files must carry a tag such as\n    # [prov-2026-1a2b3c4d] or [prov-2026-1a2b3c4d@2] (checked by the commit-msg hook).\n    commit_tag_required: false\n\n    # true: `provenance complete` runs the record's associated specs and records evidence\n    # (see `provenance check --evidence`).\n    # A spec's run_command is run as `<run_command> <path>`, or with {{path}} substituted\n    # wherever it appears (so `go test ./... -run X {{path}}` and `test -f {{path}}` both work).\n    run_associated_specs_on_complete: true\n\n    # What `complete` does when it touches files of other implemented records whose specs\n    # now fail: block, warn or off.\n    overlap_specs_on_complete: warn\n\n    # true: open, complete and deprecate commit the record change themselves.\n    commit_on_status_change: false\n\n    # false: no file is locked. true: every tracked file that no open record's scope\n    # covers is made read-only (`provenance reconcile`), which suits a project once its\n    # first records exist. Omit the key for the default, which is true.\n    write_restriction: false\n\n    # A command run in a clean checkout of every commit you push (the pre-push hook;\n    # install it with `provenance hooks install`). Leave it out to skip the check.\n    # pre_push_command: go build ./...\n\nImports, each its own addImport, exactly these: fmt, io, os, os/exec, path/filepath, strings, github.com/spf13/cobra.\n\nDeclarations, in this order, each exactly one set* call whose code kwarg is the code below verbatim (gofmt-formatted, comments kept). Do not alter, reorder or add anything.\n\n  - setFunction name initDirIsGit, code exactly:\n      func initDirIsGit(dir string) bool {\n      \tc := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", dir, \"rev-parse\", \"--is-inside-work-tree\")\n      \tc.Env = cleanGitEnv()\n      \treturn c.Run() == nil\n      }\n  - setFunction name initConfigText, code exactly:\n      func initConfigText() string {\n      \treturn initConfig\n      }\n  - setFunction name runInit, code exactly:\n      func runInit(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n      \tdirFlag, _ := cmd.Flags().GetString(\"dir\")\n      \tforce, _ := cmd.Flags().GetBool(\"force\")\n      \tif dirFlag == \"\" {\n      \t\tdirFlag = \".\"\n      \t}\n      \tdir, err := filepath.Abs(dirFlag)\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tif info, err := os.Stat(dir); err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n      \t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"--dir %q is not an existing directory\", dirFlag)\n      \t}\n      \tcfgText := initConfigText()\n      \tcfgPath := filepath.Join(dir, configFile)\n      \texisting, readErr := os.ReadFile(cfgPath)\n      \thasConfig := readErr == nil\n      \tvar lines []string\n      \tswitch {\n      \tcase hasConfig && string(existing) == cfgText:\n      \t\tlines = append(lines, \"unchanged  \"+configFile)\n      \tcase hasConfig && !force:\n      \t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s already has a %s: init does not overwrite it (use --force; the old file is saved as %s.bak)\", dir, configFile, configFile)\n      \tdefault:\n      \t\tif legacy, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dir, legacyConfigFile)); err == nil && !hasConfig && !force && strings.Contains(\"\\n\"+string(legacy), \"\\nprovenance:\") {\n      \t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s has a provenance block in %s: run provenance migrate to convert it (or use --force to write a fresh %s)\", dir, legacyConfigFile, configFile)\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tlabel := \"created    \"\n      \t\tif hasConfig {\n      \t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(cfgPath+\".bak\", existing, 0o644); err != nil {\n      \t\t\t\treturn err\n      \t\t\t}\n      \t\t\tlabel = \"overwrote  \"\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tif err := os.WriteFile(cfgPath, []byte(cfgText), 0o644); err != nil {\n      \t\t\treturn err\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tlines = append(lines, label+configFile)\n      \t}\n      \trecDir := filepath.Join(dir, \"provenance\")\n      \tif _, err := os.Stat(recDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n      \t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(recDir, 0o755); err != nil {\n      \t\t\treturn err\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(recDir, \".gitkeep\"), nil, 0o644); err != nil {\n      \t\t\treturn err\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tlines = append(lines, \"created    provenance/.gitkeep\")\n      \t}\n      \tattrStatus, err := ensureGitattributes(dir, \"provenance\")\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"%-11s.gitattributes\", attrStatus))\n      \tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"\\n✓ Initialised provenance in %s\\n\\n\", dir)\n      \tfor _, l := range lines {\n      \t\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"    %s\\n\", l)\n      \t}\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"\\nNext steps (run them yourself; init installs nothing):\\n\")\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"  1. provenance hooks install         install the pre-commit, commit-msg and pre-push git hooks\\n\")\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"  2. provenance install-skills        install the Claude Code provenance skill\\n\")\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"  3. provenance install-plugin        install the Claude Code provenance plugin\\n\")\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"  4. provenance create --type blueprint --no-edit --title \\\"...\\\"   start your first record\\n\")\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"  5. provenance next                  ask what to do next\\n\")\n      \tif !initDirIsGit(dir) {\n      \t\tfmt.Fprint(out, \"\\n  Note: this directory is not a git repository; the hooks and commit tags need git (git init).\\n\")\n      \t}\n      \tfmt.Fprint(out, \"\\n\")\n      \treturn nil\n      }\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- TestInitWritesAConfigTheLoaderKnows (strict decode into the CLI config type plus a key check) and TestInitRefusalsForceAndIdempotence pass; init installs nothing and never overwrites without --force.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\nSelect every invocation this record declares, in all its files (the init wiring, cmd/provenance/init_run.go and the others the record names): every addImport, addFlag, setConst, setFunction and wiring invocation the record states, so no region is dropped. The constant initSedumContext no longer exists and initConfigText takes no parameter; there is no sedum detection, no .sedum/context.md and no gitignore note. Follow the record's text and code as written, with nothing added.\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: describeRoot {\"bin\":\"provenance\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: addShortPersistentFlag:string {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"flag\":\"config\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"check\"} (owned by prov-2026-063f1395; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"status\"} (owned by prov-2026-12b1ca97; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"deprecate\"} (owned by prov-2026-35439261; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"complete\"} (owned by prov-2026-41fb548c; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\"} (owned by prov-2026-44a07768; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"edit\"} (owned by prov-2026-57b8a95b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"revise\"} (owned by prov-2026-5f69977b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"open\"} (owned by prov-2026-6db88b75; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"migrate\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"reconcile\"} (owned by prov-2026-9a3aad45; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"repin\"} (owned by prov-2026-9bfa6107; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"lint\"} (owned by prov-2026-a03e6bc3; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"diff\"} (owned by prov-2026-bfd55535; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"run-specs\"} (owned by prov-2026-c31c9c59; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"hooks\"} (owned by prov-2026-d1d789de; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"history\"} (owned by prov-2026-d435c27b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"stale\"} (owned by prov-2026-f476b640; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"sync\"} (owned by prov-2026-f807707a; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"next\"} (owned by prov-2026-11876813; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"evidence\"} (owned by